# PSIO-GM project conventions

## Branch
Until the user says otherwise, **all commits go to branch `v0.1`**.

## Version tags
- **Branch** for ongoing work: `v0.1`
- **Release tags** use semver patch form: `v0.1.0`, `v0.1.1`, … (never reuse the exact branch name as a tag)

## Documentation
When making meaningful changes, update repo documentation as needed:

- **CHANGELOG.md** — user-facing behaviour, fixes, features, packaging, and notable refactors (Keep a Changelog style under the current version)
- **README.md** — install/run/usage/Docker notes when those change; keep “About this fork” accurate if the fork delta changes
- **GitHub Issues** — close or update issues when work fixes them; link commits/changelog entries
- Prefer documenting *why* and user impact over restating every line of code

Skip trivial noise (typos-only, pure formatting) unless the user asks to record them.
